Subject: Identify A2DP playback profiles independently of input count

WirePlumber can expose a Bluetooth input loopback while A2DP is active.
Rejecting every profile with a source leaves working stereo profiles out
of the selection and triggers the daemon's WirePlumber recovery path.

Match the playback profile name, retaining output/availability checks and
codec ranking. Add the Fedora 44 profile layout and reject non-playback
names independently of their reported input count. Use A2DP names in the
existing codec-ranking fixtures.

Applies to harveywuk/librepods 4ed49df0b301ac3e6fba9c81dfbbb6726cc52201.

